WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.133
A2A, the Agent2Agent protocol.

2
00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:04.936
Your agent can call tools.

3
00:00:04.936 --> 00:00:08.867
But what happens when it needs to hire a completely different agent?

4
00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:14.667
A2A is an open standard that lets one agent talk to another agent.

5
00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:16.333
It was started by Google.

6
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:21.967
And it works across teams, companies, and vendors, with no custom integration for each pair.

7
00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:26.000
Most people mix these two up, so let's separate them.

8
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.633
MCP connects an agent to tools.

9
00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:30.867
A2A connects agents to each other.

10
00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.649
They are not rivals.

11
00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:37.467
A mature system uses MCP inside each agent, and A2A between them.

12
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:40.467
Here is how the exchange works.

13
00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:41.988
First, discovery.

14
00:00:41.988 --> 00:00:47.733
Each agent publishes an agent card, a small JSON file describing what it can do.

15
00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:49.208
Second, delegation.

16
00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:55.267
The caller sends a task, which moves through states like submitted, working, completed, or failed.

17
00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.200
Finally, the work comes back as an artifact.

18
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:05.267
Here is a trimmed agent card, served at a well known path ending in agent card dot json.

19
00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.967
It names the agent and gives its address.

20
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:10.433
It lists capabilities, such as streaming.

21
00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:11.984
And it lists skills.

22
00:01:11.984 --> 00:01:15.300
This is the menu other agents read before delegating.

23
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.733
Here's a real case.

24
00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:22.367
A partner team's launch agent needs space weather clearance for a launch window.

25
00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:26.233
It fetches your agent card and sees the space weather brief skill.

26
00:01:26.533 --> 00:01:30.152
It delegates the task, and a structured brief comes back.

27
00:01:30.152 --> 00:01:32.311
Neither team wrote an integration.

28
00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:34.533
Both just implemented the standard.

29
00:01:35.733 --> 00:01:36.626
Let's recap.

30
00:01:36.626 --> 00:01:38.933
A2A lets agents talk to agents.

31
00:01:39.233 --> 00:01:42.467
The agent card advertises what an agent can do.

32
00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:46.267
Work moves as tasks, and results come back as artifacts.

33
00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:49.979
MCP is for tools, A2A is between agents.

34
00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:51.600
Next up: LangChain.
